settings {
  book_writing_llm: ollama local model ornith-1.5:35b
  book_directory: {directory_of_this_prompt}/../.chat/books
  words_per_chapter: 400
  number_of_chapters: 15
  sub_questions_to_ask_when_planning: 10
  sub_questions_article_search_limit: 10
}

task.find_word_in_book (completed) {
  please implement a "Find" component on top of the book loader modal, allow me the find words in the book
}

task.blocking_detection (completed) {
  currently, before we write a book, we will search different sub questions with /news search
  for each news article fetching, please indidate whether ths article content fetching is successful or not
  if we encountered:
  ```
  We're sorry...
  ... but your computer or network may be sending automated queries. To protect our users, we can't process your request right now.

  See Google Help for more information.
  ```
  simply say "blocked by google news"

  if there are blocking policies presented in individual website, simply say "blocked by website"

  please also show the url of each article that's being fetched during this process
}

task.remove.articles_to_learn (completed) {
  remove the usage of articles_to_learn in the settings form
  we will no longer use settings.articles_to_learn, instead, we just rely on settings.sub_questions_to_ask_when_planning and settins.sub_questions_article_search_limit 
}

task.expose_settings_in_form (completed) {
  - update {settings}:
  - after tying /write_a_book, expose all {settings} options to the form and allow me to customize them, there will be no maximum of each setting options
}

task.refactor (completed) {
  - update {settings}
  - when planning, think about {settings.sub_questions_to_ask_when_planning}, for each sub_question:
    - articles: search {settings.sub_questions_article_search_limit} articles equally
    - add {articles} to the book writing references
  - when writing the book, think about all of the {articles} are related, discover ideas by connecting them with creative thinking
}

task.evenly_distributed_horizontal_search (completed) {
  for all questions we come up when planning to write a book:
  make sure the search results are evenly reflecting every single one of the question
}

task.more_horizontal_exploration (completed) {
  currently, it seems like when planning to write a book, it will come up with 6 different questions to search for the articles, please come with up 10 different quetions to search instead
}

task.do_not_include_2024 (completed) {
  when searching online articles, often times, i found that we tries to search year 2024 topics:
  for example:
  - Prompting techniques for large language models 2024
  please DO NOT do that, we should focus on year 2025 and year 2026
}

task (completed) {
  update {words_per_chapter}
  update {max_number_of_chapters}
  update {articles_to_learn}
}

task.ask_question_before_writing_book (completed) {
  after typing /write_a_book:
  - ask me the following question:
  - words per chapter (default {words_per_chapter})
  - number of chapter (default {max_number_of_chapters})
  - articles to learn (default {articles_to_learn})
}

task.load_a_book (completed) {
  reference task.books_command:
  - when clicking on each book url, open up a modal and show the book content, similar to opening up individual news search result
}

task.keywords (completed) {
  once we have the keywords, when searching like /news search, add plus sign between keywords:
  for example:
  keywords: japan driving guide for beginner 
  actual keywords: japan+driving+guide+for+beginner
}

task (completed) {
  update {articles_to_learn}
}

task (completed) {
  reference task.write_a_book:
  - for lists_of_knowledge, learn from /news search {keywords}, but only target on results that are from the pass 2 years only, only extract top {articles_to_learn} results
}

task (completed) {
  reference task.write_a_book:
  - update {book_directory}  
  - each book should have between 3 to {max_number_of_chapters}
  - each chapter should have about {words_per_chapter}
}

task.write_a_book (completed) {
  command: /write_a_book <subject> {
    keywords: based on <subject>, use {book_writing_llm} to construct one list of keywords i should search
    lists_of_knowledge: learn from /new search {keywords}, but only target on results that are from the pass 2 years only, only extract top 10 results
    learn all the text in {lists_of_knowledge}
    write a book chapter by chapter, each chapter has maximum 600 words
    save the book to {book_directory}/{subject}.html
  }
}

task.books_command (completed) {
  create a command: /books {
    - list all the books in {book_directory}
  }
}
